[2026-03-14T18:55:40.991Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JEF9ZSMtuNSqDANyboSDnm","type":"tool_result","content":"   600→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, navigates to `/team/eng-1/issues` for team \"Engineering\"\n   601→- **Expected**: The page displays a header with the team name \"Engineering\" and an \"Issues\" label. A \"New Issue\" button is visible in the header area.\n   602→\n   603→#### Test: Team Issues page shows issues grouped by status (default)\n   604→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has issues in Backlog (3), In Progress (2), Done (1)\n   605→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under status headers. Each group header shows the status icon, status name, and issue count in parentheses. Groups appear in status order: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled. Empty status groups are not displayed.\n   606→\n   607→#### Test: Team Issues page shows all team issues, not just current user's\n   608→- **Initial state**: User \"Alice\" is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has issues: ENG-1 (assigned to Alice), ENG-2 (assigned to Bob), ENG-3 (unassigned)\n   609→- **Expected**: All three issues (ENG-1, ENG-2, ENG-3) are visible on the team issues page.\n   610→\n   611→#### Test: Team Issues page shows empty state when team has no issues\n   612→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has no issues\n   613→- **Expected**: A friendly empty state message with an icon is displayed (e.g., \"No issues yet. Create your first issue to get started.\") and the \"New Issue\" button is visible.\n   614→\n   615→#### Test: Issue row displays all required fields including checkbox and team prefix\n   616→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues. Issue ENG-42 exists with title \"Fix login bug\", status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", labels [\"Bug\"], assignee \"Jane Doe\" (with avatar), due date \"2026-03-20\", project \"Auth Rewrite\".\n   617→- **Expected**: The issue row displays: a checkbox for bulk selection (unchecked), High priority icon (orange arrow-up), identifier \"ENG-42\" with team prefix, title \"Fix login bug\", In Progress status icon (yellow half circle), \"Bug\" label as a small colored badge, assignee avatar, due date \"Mar 20\", and project name \"Auth Rewrite\".\n   618→\n   619→#### Test: Issue row title is clickable and navigates to issue detail\n   620→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with issue ENG-42\n   621→- **Action**: User clicks on the title \"Fix login bug\" in the issue row\n   622→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/issue/<issueId>` for issue ENG-42.\n   623→\n   624→#### Test: Issue row status icon is clickable to change status\n   625→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues. Issue ENG-42 has status \"Todo\".\n   626→- **Action**: User clicks the status icon on the ENG-42 issue row\n   627→- **Expected**: A dropdown/popover appears showing all available statuses (Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled) with their respective icons and colors.\n   628→\n   629→#### Test: Changing status via issue row status dropdown persists and moves issue between groups\n   630→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues grouped by status. \"Todo\" group has ENG-42. \"In Progress\" group has 1 issue.\n   631→- **Action**: User clicks the status icon on ENG-42, selects \"In Progress\" from the dropdown\n   632→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. ENG-42 moves from the \"Todo\" group to the \"In Progress\" group. Group counts update accordingly. The change is persisted to the database.\n   633→\n   634→#### Test: Issue row status dropdown can be used multiple times\n   635→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has status \"Todo\"\n   636→- **Action**: User clicks status icon, changes to \"In Progress\", then clicks status icon again, changes to \"Done\"\n   637→- **Expected**: Both status changes work correctly. The issue ends up in the \"Done\" group with a green check circle icon. Each dropdown opens and closes cleanly.\n   638→\n   639→#### Test: Status group headers are collapsible\n   640→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"In Progress\" group is expanded with 2 issues\n   641→- **Action**: User clicks the \"In Progress\" group header\n   642→- **Expected**: The group collapses, hiding all issues within it. The group header remains visible with a collapse indicator (e.g., chevron rotates). Clicking again expands the group back.\n   643→\n   644→#### Test: Status group collapse toggles multiple times\n   645→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Backlog\" group is expanded with 3 issues\n   646→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Backlog\" header to collapse, clicks it again to expand, then collapses once more\n   647→- **Expected**: Each click toggles correctly. After three clicks, the group is collapsed and its issues are hidden. The count in parentheses remains accurate.\n   648→\n   649→#### Test: Multiple status groups can be independently collapsed\n   650→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog, In Progress, and Done groups, all expanded\n   651→- **Action**: User collapses the \"Backlog\" group, then collapses the \"Done\" group\n   652→- **Expected**: \"Backlog\" and \"Done\" groups are collapsed while \"In Progress\" remains expanded showing its issues.\n   653→\n   654→#### Test: Issue row displays priority icon with correct color\n   655→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with issues at different priorities\n   656→- **Expected**: Urgent shows red alert-triangle icon, High shows orange arrow-up, Medium shows yellow minus, Low shows blue arrow-down, No Priority shows gray dots-horizontal.\n   657→\n   658→#### Test: Issue row displays labels as colored badges\n   659→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has labels