 (e.g., ENG-44). The group count updates.\n   683→\n   684→### BulkActions\n   685→\n   686→#### Test: Issue row checkboxes are visible and unchecked by default\n   687→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with 5 issues\n   688→- **Expected**: Each issue row has a checkbox on the left side. All checkboxes are unchecked by default.\n   689→\n   690→#### Test: Clicking a checkbox selects an issue\n   691→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with ENG-42 unchecked\n   692→- **Action**: User clicks the checkbox on ENG-42\n   693→- **Expected**: The checkbox becomes checked. The issue row has a selected visual style (e.g., highlighted background). A bulk action toolbar appears at the top or bottom of the list.\n   694→\n   695→#### Test: Clicking a checked checkbox deselects the issue\n   696→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 checkbox is checked, bulk action toolbar is visible\n   697→- **Action**: User clicks the checkbox on ENG-42 again\n   698→- **Expected**: The checkbox becomes unchecked. The selected visual style is removed from the row. If no other issues are selected, the bulk action toolbar disappears.\n   699→\n   700→#### Test: Multiple issues can be selected via checkboxes\n   701→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with ENG-42, ENG-43, ENG-44\n   702→- **Action**: User clicks checkboxes on ENG-42 and ENG-44\n   703→- **Expected**: Both ENG-42 and ENG-44 are checked with selected visual style. ENG-43 remains unchecked. The bulk action toolbar shows \"2 selected\" or similar count indicator.\n   704→\n   705→#### Test: Bulk action toolbar appears when issues are selected\n   706→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no issues selected, no bulk action toolbar visible\n   707→- **Action**: User clicks the checkbox on ENG-42\n   708→- **Expected**: A bulk action toolbar appears showing the selection count (\"1 selected\") and action buttons for: Status change, Priority change, Assignee change, and Label change.\n   709→\n   710→#### Test: Bulk action toolbar disappears when all issues are deselected\n   711→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 is selected, bulk action toolbar is visible\n   712→- **Action**: User unchecks ENG-42\n   713→- **Expected**: The bulk action toolbar disappears. No action buttons are visible.\n   714→\n   715→#### Test: Bulk status change updates all selected issues\n   716→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 (status \"Todo\") and ENG-43 (status \"Backlog\") are selected via checkboxes\n   717→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" action in the bulk toolbar, selects \"In Progress\" from the dropdown\n   718→- **Expected**: Both ENG-42 and ENG-43 are updated to \"In Progress\" status. They move to the \"In Progress\" group. The changes are persisted to the database. The checkboxes are deselected and the bulk toolbar disappears.\n   719→\n   720→#### Test: Bulk priority change updates all selected issues\n   721→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 (priority \"Low\") and ENG-43 (priority \"Medium\") are selected\n   722→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Priority\" action in the bulk toolbar, selects \"High\" from the dropdown\n   723→- **Expected**: Both issues are updated to \"High\" priority. The priority icons change to orange arrow-up on both rows. Changes are persisted to the database.\n   724→\n   725→#### Test: Bulk assignee change updates all selected issues\n   726→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 (assigned to Alice) and ENG-43 (unassigned) are selected\n   727→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Assignee\" action in the bulk toolbar, selects \"Bob\" from the member selector\n   728→- **Expected**: Both issues are now assigned to Bob. The assignee avatars update on both rows. Changes are persisted to the database.\n   729→\n   730→#### Test: Bulk label change updates all selected issues\n   731→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 (no labels) and ENG-43 (label \"Bug\") are selected\n   732→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" action in the bulk toolbar, selects \"Feature\" from the label picker\n   733→- **Expected**: Both issues now have the \"Feature\" label. ENG-43 retains its existing \"Bug\" label and also gains \"Feature\". Label badges update on both rows. Changes are persisted.\n   734→\n   735→#### Test: Bulk actions can be performed multiple times in sequence\n   736→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with multiple issues\n   737→- **Action**: User selects ENG-42 and ENG-43, bulk-changes status to \"In Progress\", then selects ENG-44 and ENG-45, bulk-changes priority to \"High\"\n   738→- **Expected**: Both bulk actions complete successfully. The first pair is in \"In Progress\" status, the second pair has \"High\" priority. The bulk toolbar appears and disappears correctly each time.\n   739→\n   740→#### Test: Select all checkbox in group header selects all issues in that group\n   741→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Backlog\" group has 3 issues, none selected\n   742→- **Action**: User clicks a \"select all\" checkbox in the \"Backlog\" group header\n   743→- **Expected**: All 3 issues in the Backlog group are selected (checkboxes checked, selected visual style). The bulk toolbar shows \"3 selected\". Issues in other groups remain unselected.\n   744→\n   745→#### Test: Deselect all via group header checkbox\n   746→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, all 3 issues in \"Backlog\" group are selected via group header checkbox\n   747→- **Action**: User clicks the group header checkbox again\n   748→- **Expected**: All 3 issues are deselected. If no other issues are selected, the bulk toolbar disappears.\n   749→\n   750→### GroupBySort\n   751→\n   752→#### Test: Group by control renders with default \"Status\" selected\n   753→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   754→- **Expected**: A \"Group by\" control/dropdown is visible in the toolbar area. It shows \"Status\" as the currently selected grouping option.\n   755→\n   756→#### Test: Group by dropdown shows all grouping options\n   757→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   758→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Group by\" control\n   759→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing options: Status, Priority, Assignee, Project, Label, None. Each option is clickable.\n   760→\n   761→#### Test: Group by Priority groups issues under priority headers\n   762→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with priorities: Urgent (1), High (2), Medium (1), Low (1), No Priority (1)\n   763→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from the Group by dropdown\n   764→- **Expected**: Issues are regrouped under priority headers: Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No Priority. Each header shows the priority icon, name, and count. Empty priority groups are not shown.\n   765→\n   766→#### Test: Group by Assignee groups issues under assignee headers\n   767→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues assigned to Alice (2), Bob (1), and unassigned (1)\n   768→- **Action**: User selects \"Assignee\" from the Group by dropdown\n   769→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under assignee name headers with their avatars. An \"Unassigned\" group shows issues with no assignee. Each header shows the assignee avatar, name, and issue count.\n   770→\n   771→#### Test: Group by Project groups issues under project headers\n   772→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in project \"Auth Rewrite\" (2), \"Dashboard v2\" (1), and no project (1)\n   773→- **Action**: User selects \"Project\" from the Group by dropdown\n   774→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under project name headers. A \"No Project\" group shows unassigned issues. Each header shows the project name and issue count.\n   775→\n   776→#### Test: Group by Label groups issues under label headers\n   777→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with labels \"Bug\" (2), \"Feature\" (1), and no labels (1)\n   778→- **Action**: User selects \"Label\" from the Group by dropdown\n   779→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under label name headers with colored dots. A \"No Label\" group shows unlabeled issues. Issues with multiple labels appear under each applicable label group.\n   780→\n   781→#### Test: Group by None shows a flat list\n   782→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has 6 issues in various statuses\n   783→- **Action**: User selects \"None\" from the Group by dropdown\n   784→- **Expected**: All issues are displayed in a flat list without any group headers. Issues are shown in the current sort order.\n   785→\n   786→#### Test: Switching group by option re-renders immediately\n   787→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issues are grouped by Status\n   788→- **Action**: User changes Group by from \"Status\" to \"Priority\"\n   789→- **Expected**: The issue list immediately re-renders with priority-based grouping. No page reload is needed. The transition is smooth.\n   790→\n   791→#### Test: Group by can be changed multiple times\n   792→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   793→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" grouping, then \"Assignee\", then back to \"Status\"\n   794→- **Expected**: Each change correctly re-groups the issues. After returning to \"Status\", the view matches the original default grouping.\n   795→\n   796→#### Test: Sort by control renders with default option\n   797→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   798→- **Expected**: A \"Sort by\" control/dropdown is visible in the toolbar area, showing the current sort option.\n   799→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef08a80e-9f91-4113-ac94-4aa63f198c9e","uuid":"9b4f3dc3-515c-4980-848e-c0ecdd3dc798","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/Li